INSTALLATION:

    To install this fine program, you must copy both the "Upload_Lister" and 
    "Upload_Lister.config" files to a specific directory. This directory 
    must be in your "DOORS:" directory, and must be named "DOORS:Upload_Lister"

eg. DOORS:Upload_Lister/Upload_Lister
    DOORS:Upload_Lister/Upload_Lister.config


*NOTE* For this door to have any hope of working, you must have the two files 
       "Upload_Lister" and "Upload_Lister.config" in the "DOORS:Upload_Lister"
       directory.

    Then go about configuring your menus, ie edit one of your ????menu.text 
    files, also under configure menus, set a key and function 34, 
    (door function), then set the correct path in FILENAME/PATHS etc.

eg. KEY:  FUNCTION:  EXTRA:   LO:   HI:     FILENAME/NAME/DEST/PATH
     U       34        0       0   10000    DOORS:Upload_Lister/Upload_Lister



CONFIGURING:

    This version of the Upload Lister now comes with a configuration file,
    Upload_Lister.config. 

eg. 5000           ;SYSOP ACCESS LEVEL, has to be used!!!
    John Dowe      ;Optional USER NAME who you want hidden sections for
    32 23 20       ;Optional HIDDEN SECTIONS for above user
    Mary Q Citizen ;Optional USER NAME who you want hidden sections for
    21             ;Optional HIDDEN SECTIONS for above user


*NOTE* The above file has to appear exactly as shown, without the
       comments, to work correctly.


ie. 5000
    John Dowe
    32 23 20
    Mary Q Citizen
    21 


    The minimum amount of information within the file is the SYSOP ACCESS
    LEVEL, ie the file must have the SYSOP ACCESS LEVEL for this door to
    work, the USER NAMES and HIDDEN SECTIONS are optional.

eg. 5000
    

    The USERS' NAMES are an optional field that must be an exact replica of 
    the NAMES contained in MAX's BBS config files. The maximum length of these 
    NAMES is 80 chars. The maximum number of NAMES is only limited by your 
    maximum file size. If a USER'S NAME field exists then you must have a 
    HIDDEN SECTIONS field, as below.
  

    The HIDDEN SECTIONS are values that range from 1-255, that must be
    seperated by a space. The maximum number off HIDDEN SECTIONS, is the
    amount of HIDDEN SECTIONS that will fit on an 80 char line.



COMPILING:

    I used SAS 6.2 to compile this, but it's pretty portable code, (where have
    you heard that one before :-), I have included the scoptions file.



WHY DID I DO IT?:

    Well I don't know about anyone else but I was finding it mighty difficult 
    to remember all the different files I had uploaded to all the different 
    BBS's. There's three solutions, (that I know off):

            1. Just let the BBS spit the dummy after you've uploaded a file 
               that already existed on the BBS. Real Kludgy and a big waste 
               of bandwidth as well.


            2. Write your own logging software, script, Arexx, C, etc, that 
               keeps obviously a log of all files uploaded and to whom.
               This one is a good idea, just too much work :-)


            3. Do what I did, download the MAX's BBS software, write your own 
               door starter code, and code away. A door is an external program 
               running on the BBS machine, that somehow enhances the running 
               off the BBS, by allowing more options, greater functionality, 
               or more entertainment that the BBS on its own could allow. 
               Perfect example is most of the online games that you play.



HOW IT WORKS:

    This software is in fact very simple, all it does is read the file.data 
    file, into memory, searching for any files it finds that have been uploaded 
    by the current user. In other words giving an upload file listing instead 
    of just the number that you normally get to see. The one problem with this 
    method, is that if the file, file.data is really big, (>200K), and you have 
    limited memory, then the code will not be able to allocate the required 
    memory and hence EXIT gracefully, the advantage of this method, is that 
    it's very quick. If enough, (any?), people ask, (complain), then I'll write 
    a more generic one for those machines with lots of users, but only small 
    amounts of memory.


    The files that should be included are:

         Upload_Lister        - 17800 bytes  ;Ari's Amiga Executable V 1.00
         Upload_Lister.config -    51 bytes  ;Configuration file for door
         Upload_Lister.doc    -  8999 bytes  ;I'm typing it, you're reading it!
         



VERSIONS:

    V 1.00 -Final Version, unless someone starts paying me ;-). It will now 
            respond to a TWIT perfectly, old doorpack had some serious 
            limitations and bugs so I wrote my own. Doorpack is still good, 
            if you're just learning though! Also SAS 6.0/6.2 have a buggy 
            fstat() command, a real PAIN IN THE BUTT!!!!. Though stat() works 
            perfectly! Assign no longer needed, back to hard-coded directory,
            "DOORS:Upload_Lister"

    V 0.10 -Added "Upload_Lister:" as the logical name of the directory where 
            the two files "Upload_Lister" and "Upload_Lister.config", must 
            reside. This allows the SYSOP to put this door in any directory 
            they want.
	   -Added a find option for those uploaders, (SYSOPS), who have
            REALLY BIG upload lists!

    V 0.08 -Added config file, see above, which allows for user's who need
            hidden sections ;-). Also added SYSOP ACCESS LEVEL to config
            file.

    V 0.07 -Colour now works, V0.06 didn't work because there's a bad bug
            in the doorpack stuff. If you do a sendmessage with more than
            80 or so chars, you'll get a 8100 0005 guru every time. My
            BW routines were <=80 chars, but as soon as I added colour, 
            ***BOOM***.

    V 0.06 -Finally added Colour!!!

    V 0.05 -Fixed "file.data" search routine, it was hardcoded in V 0.02, now 
            it finds it from MaxsBBS.Config. Only requirement is that 
            MaxsBBS.config is in the same directory as MaxsBBS.
           -Added the capability for Sysop's to use any one's name in the 
            search for uploaded lists. The only requirement is that the 
            Sysop's ACCESS LEVEL is equal to or bigger than 5000.
           -For long lists, this door can now be aborted.


    V 0.02 -Fixed printing routine, which was displaying files one step ahead.
           -Added length, No. of downloads, file section, and file description
            to printing routines.
           -Prints in same format as most other File Listers.
           -Code cleaned up a bit, more comments added.
           -Some people were having problems with the TWIT function from 
            MaxsBBS, just press "S", after you've twited someone, and control 
            goes back to MaxsBBS.

    V 0.01 -Initial release.



